# Runbook - Deploiement {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Memo operationnel pour la stack Hetzner (preview = prod). Pour les decisions d'architecture, voir [`specs/deploy-hetzner.md`](../specs/deploy-hetzner.md).

## Architecture

```
{{#if HAS_DB}}
Internet --> Caddy :80/:443 (TLS auto Let's Encrypt) --> Next.js :3000 --> Postgres :5432
                                                              |
                                                              +--> volume "uploads" (/app/data/uploads)
{{/if HAS_DB}}
{{#if !HAS_DB}}
Internet --> Caddy :80/:443 (TLS auto Let's Encrypt) --> Next.js :3000
                                                              |
                                                              +--> volume "uploads" (/app/data/uploads)
{{/if !HAS_DB}}
```

- VPS : Hetzner Cloud CX23 ({{HETZNER_LOCATION}}), Debian 12, 2 vCPU, 4 GB RAM.
{{#if HAS_DB}}
- 3 services Docker : `db` (Postgres 17), `app` (Next.js standalone), `caddy` (reverse proxy + TLS).
- Volumes persistants : `pgdata`, `uploads`, `caddy_data`, `caddy_config`.
- Postgres bind sur `127.0.0.1:5432` du host (loopback) pour permettre au runner GHA de tunneler via SSH (`prisma migrate deploy`).
{{/if HAS_DB}}
{{#if !HAS_DB}}
- 2 services Docker : `app` (Next.js standalone), `caddy` (reverse proxy + TLS).
- Volumes persistants : `uploads`, `caddy_data`, `caddy_config`.
{{/if !HAS_DB}}
- Aucun port public hors :80/:443 - applique au niveau reseau par le **Hetzner Cloud Firewall** `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-public-web` (cf. § Modifier le firewall). SSH uniquement via Tailscale.

